description:
Add a new method on the `JmapBackend` trait that exposes the caller's stable identity to JMAP method handlers and backends. Default impl returns `None` so existing backends (with `type CallerCtx = ()`) compile unchanged.

Site: crate-jmap-server/src/backend.rs in the `JmapBackend` trait definition (around line 555-700).

Method signature:

    /// The caller's stable identity within this account namespace.
    ///
    /// Returns `None` for deployments that have not wired identity
    /// (test fixtures, single-user dev servers). A `None`-returning
    /// backend CANNOT honor JMAP semantics that depend on caller
    /// identity — chat role-hierarchy, calendar ACLs, sharing/myRights,
    /// per-user $seen on shared mailboxes, metadata isPrivate
    /// visibility scoping, etc. Authentication is still the HTTP
    /// layer's job; this method exposes the result of that
    /// authentication to the JMAP layer for in-method semantics.
    ///
    /// Implementations MUST NOT mint identity — they MUST read it
    /// from the `CallerCtx` populated by the HTTP/auth middleware
    /// before `dispatch()` was called.
    ///
    /// Backends that honor identity-dependent semantics MUST override
    /// this method. Handlers and downstream backend traits MAY rely on
    /// it being correct when it returns `Some`.
    fn principal_id(caller: &Self::CallerCtx) -> Option<&jmap_types::Id> {
        let _ = caller;
        None
    }

## Acceptance

  - Method added to `JmapBackend` trait with the doc comment above (verbatim).
  - `cargo test --workspace` clean (default impl preserves current behavior; no existing backend needs changes).
  - `cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings` clean.
  - `cargo doc -p jmap-server --no-deps` clean (RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings').
  - One unit test in jmap-server confirming the default impl returns `None` for `type CallerCtx = ()`.
  - No changes to any extension server crate (mail, chat, calendars, tasks, contacts, sharing, filenode, metadata) — verified by clippy + test passing across the workspace.

## Out of scope

  - AGENTS.md updates (→ JMAP-ga0q.2)
  - Any consumer overriding the default (chat-server backend gating lives in JMAP-g7wu.2.4.3)
  - PrincipalId newtype — explicitly rejected in the design discussion. `Id` is the JMAP wire identifier; principal_id is just an Id with a doc-comment-defined role.

## Depends on

  None. Foundation-only change.
